# Demon Wall: "As long as this creature has a counter on it, it can attack as though it didn't have defender" (CR 609.4) is
# judged as attackers are declared (CR 508.1a). Bot1's Wall gets two +1/+1 counters on turn 3. On turn 5, in the beginning of
# combat step, Bot2 sacrifices Vampire Hexmage to remove them all: with no counter left, defender stops the Wall attacking
# (the refusal, CR 702.3b) while the Ornithopter beside it attacks (the control). In the second main phase Bot1 pays {5}{B}
# again, and on turn 7 the Wall attacks as a 5/5: Bot2 goes from 20 to 15.

